        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U1 pin 6 (A) and pin 7 (B) both labelled 'TTL'"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Bias/pull network on the MAX3485 A/B differential lines and DE/RE enable line"}
      ],
      "impact": "Shorting A and B prevents the transceiver from producing a valid single-ended/differential signal, so serial-mode servos would not communicate.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The MAX3485's A and B pins are both tied to the same 'TTL' net, shorting the differential pair; this would prevent serial-mode servo communication. Confidence is limited because the spec's 'shared single-wire TTL serial bus' wording could be read as intending a single-wire node."
}

